"""Frozen opt-ins for source-proven rail/comparison composition repairs.

This is not an all-horizontal style or graph rewrite. Literal five/six-stage
rails use three tracks per row; five-stage continuation rows need centering.
Four independent peer choices use a two-by-two grid. The three-mechanism DNS
comparison fits three columns at the existing largest authored density.
Other named rails retain their columns and intact nested boundaries, including
canary chronology, account ownership and forks. The OSI five-stage rail keeps
its exact descending layer order; no feedback or hierarchy edge is invented.

Merge corpus_flow_balance_profile(include) into the existing fixed, typography,
phase-flow and group-inset profile BEFORE Layout.measure(). Merge nested maps
rather than replacing existing columns. Layout.draw() must consume the exact
center_partial_rows opt-in for both literal rail and peer-grid partial rows;
measurement and row heights remain text-driven. Center existing-width tracks,
not enlarged cards; route existing connectors to the relocated endpoint bounds.
No new return edge, peer-to-peer edge, source edit or font override is authorized.

Evidence references identify source/pixel triage records, not visual approval.
The source-key, heading and edge-label snapshots below bind every target to the
current preserved semantic DOM. Static fit/semantic tests do not approve pixels.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

from dataclasses import dataclass


